WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:01.984
"Ha-ha!"

2
00:00:01.985 --> 00:00:09.874
At first Scrooge saw only blackness, but then the sound of a man's laughter rang out.

3
00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:15.243
"That laugh sounds familiar," Scrooge thought.

4
00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:20.559
Soon his vision cleared, and he saw that he was in a bright room filled with people.

5
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.964
His nephew, Fred, was holding his belly, laughing heartily.

6
00:00:26.965 --> 00:00:33.012
His laughter was contagious, and soon his wife started laughing too.

7
00:00:33.013 --> 00:00:40.842
So did the other people gathered in the room, adults and children alike.

8
00:00:40.843 --> 00:00:45.954
"He said that Christmas was a humbug and dismissed me," Fred said.

9
00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:48.611
"Can you believe it?"

10
00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:53.128
"That's what I said earlier!" Scrooge realized.

11
00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:56.728
Was Fred talking about him?

12
00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:02.302
"I can believe he'd say those things," his wife said, her laughter fading.

13
00:01:02.303 --> 00:01:07.139
"That man can't see the good in anything."

14
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:15.278
Scrooge was startled to hear Fred's wife insult him that way, as she was generally a kind and polite woman.

15
00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:19.140
"He's a comical old fellow, that's the truth," Fred said.

16
00:01:19.141 --> 00:01:23.089
"He's not as pleasant or as kind as he could be, that's for sure.

17
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.931
However, I try not to judge others."

18
00:01:26.932 --> 00:01:29.890
His wife's sister rolled her eyes.

19
00:01:29.891 --> 00:01:38.166
"I'll judge Ebenezer Scrooge for you then. His only good quality is his wealth!"

20
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:43.655
Fred shrugged. "My uncle's wealth is of no use to him.

21
00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:46.143
He doesn't do any good with it.

22
00:01:46.144 --> 00:01:49.258
He doesn't even make himself comfortable with it.

23
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:55.719
He lives in that small, dreary apartment and hoards his money, which can't possibly make him happy."

24
00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:59.505
"I have no patience with him," his wife said.

25
00:01:59.506 --> 00:02:03.662
Her sister and several others nodded their agreement.

26
00:02:03.663 --> 00:02:09.803
Fred smiled at them. "I feel sorry for him, which means I can't stay very angry with him.

27
00:02:09.804 --> 00:02:14.426
I mean, who suffers from his bad temper? He does!

28
00:02:14.427 --> 00:02:21.061
For example, he has decided to dislike us, so he won't come and dine with us, even on Christmas.

29
00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:29.988
What's the consequence? He misses out on a good dinner and some pleasant moments that he might actually enjoy."

30
00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:38.276
"Your uncle's company might do us harm," a young man called out, which made several other guests laugh again.

31
00:02:38.277 --> 00:02:45.717
"I give my poor old uncle the same invitation every year," Fred said, "whether he likes it or not.

32
00:02:45.718 --> 00:02:50.219
I certainly don't make his mood any worse by showing up at his office."

33
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:56.659
His wife nodded. "That's true. His mood is always foul!

34
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:03.006
It's a shame that your kindness, though, doesn't inspire him to help his poor clerk somehow."

35
00:03:03.007 --> 00:03:07.404
"Speaking of Bob Cratchit, I saw him earlier today," Fred said.

36
00:03:07.405 --> 00:03:12.306
"He was carrying that little son of his, the one they call Tiny Tim."

37
00:03:12.307 --> 00:03:16.006
"Oh, that poor boy," a woman said.

38
00:03:16.007 --> 00:03:22.396
"He's been sickly since the day he was born. But he's such a sweet child!"

39
00:03:22.397 --> 00:03:26.584
"Indeed he is." Fred shook his head.

40
00:03:26.585 --> 00:03:31.244
"Today Tiny Tim couldn't stop talking about seeing the ice skaters in the park.

41
00:03:31.245 --> 00:03:35.044
And he told me all about a big turkey in one of the shops."

42
00:03:35.045 --> 00:03:39.986
Fred smiled briefly before his expression went serious again.

43
00:03:39.987 --> 00:03:46.848
"Tiny Tim didn't look well. I fear the boy doesn't have long to live."

44
00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:53.495
His wife turned to gaze at their own children, who were playing at the other end of the room.

45
00:03:53.496 --> 00:03:57.423
"Oh no," she said softly.

46
00:03:57.424 --> 00:04:01.861
She brushed away a few tears before turning back to the others.

47
00:04:01.862 --> 00:04:10.300
"Fred, we've turned things far too solemn for Christmas. Let's have some fun."

48
00:04:10.301 --> 00:04:23.947
Scrooge watched as the group played music and sang songs together.

49
00:04:23.948 --> 00:04:29.298
After that, everyone played games, with the children joining in.

50
00:04:29.299 --> 00:04:35.006
Scrooge had always been impatient with games, which he considered a waste of time.

51
00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:42.847
But tonight he couldn't stop himself from smiling as Fred and his guests enjoyed themselves.

52
00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:46.123
One of the games was called Yes and No.

53
00:04:46.124 --> 00:04:52.181
Fred announced that he was thinking of something, and that the others had to figure out what it was.

54
00:04:52.182 --> 00:04:57.222
However, he could only answer their questions with a simple "yes" or "no."

55
00:04:57.223 --> 00:05:01.638
"Are you thinking of a beast?" a tall woman called out.

56
00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:04.869
"Yes!" Fred replied.

57
00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:08.881
"Is it something we might serve for dinner?"

58
00:05:08.882 --> 00:05:11.180
"No!"

59
00:05:11.181 --> 00:05:13.827
"Is it a savage animal?"

60
00:05:13.828 --> 00:05:16.366
"Yes!"

61
00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:19.254
"Does it grunt?"

62
00:05:19.255 --> 00:05:21.589
"Yes!"

63
00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:26.191
"Is it scary?" a child asked with a shiver.

64
00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:28.751
"Yes!"

65
00:05:28.752 --> 00:05:34.611
"I know who it is!" Fred's sister-in-law clapped her hands and grinned.

66
00:05:34.612 --> 00:05:44.264
"I know exactly the beast you're thinking of, Fred! It's your uncle Scrooge!"

67
00:05:44.265 --> 00:05:50.114
Everyone at the party, including Fred, burst into loud laughter.

68
00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:52.857
But Scrooge frowned.

69
00:05:52.858 --> 00:06:00.898
Fred's sister-in-law had just called him a scary beast!

